 "decisions": {
  "FT-aimnet": "AIMNet2 with the aimnet package parts (model yaml aimnet2_dftd3_wb97m + weights of the released aimnet2_wb97m_d3_0.jpt, SizeGroupedDataset / Sampler, MTLoss energy_loss_fn + peratom_loss_fn, Forces, pt2jpt export helpers) and a loop here (aimnet train needs wandb for metrics and has no time budget). D3 head switched to B3LYP-D3(BJ) (s8 1.9889, a1 0.3981, a2 4.4211) = the label dispersion, so the network only learns the electronic difference. Molecular charge input = the structure's total_charge (D1 all 0; D0 has total -2 / +1 reactions) in training, E0 fit, export check and FT-1. Loss weights energy 1 : forces 0.2 (aimnet default_train.yaml, partial-charges term dropped: no label partial charges), RAdam lr 1e-4 (default 4e-4 is from scratch), grad clip 0.4, ReduceLROnPlateau 0.75 / 3.",
  "FT-E0": "atomic reference energies by least squares: E0(Z) = E0_foundation(Z) + lstsq(counts, E_fit - E_foundation) on the training structures (<= 40,000, all structures with a rare element kept) \u2014 the formula of mace.data.estimate_e0s_from_foundation (MACE --E0s=estimated); MACE --E0s=average (verified in mace/data/utils.compute_average_E0s: lstsq of total energies on atom counts) would double count the foundation's interaction energy because load_foundations_elements copies the foundation scale/shift. AIMNet2: the same residual least squares with the pretrained atomic shifts zeroed (= aimnet SAE, mode linreg).",
  "FT-frame": "training energy E_fit = REF_energy - sum ATOM_REF_EH[Z] x EH2EV (fixed, rounded per-element constants): float32 total energies of ~2-7e4 eV are quantised at 2-8 meV (0.05-0.18 kcal/mol, Br worst); the shift keeps |E_fit| ~ 1e2 eV (spacing ~1e-5 eV). Forces untouched. Export adds ATOM_REF back to the E0s, so exported models predict absolute label-level energies (eV).",
